      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 American Society for Reproductive Medicine. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Dysmenorrhea as a reason to initiate estroprogestins is significantly more common in women with endometriosis than in women without the disease. This might explain the previously reported mild association between endometriosis and past use of oral contraceptives."
